  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This strong cultivar brings a lot of color to the garden landscape. The spring and early summer coloration is a striking orange red, which shades from light to dark Corvallis with a spread of 10 cm. The lobes are long-ovate, tapering to a slender point, and divided two-thirds of the way to the leaf base. The edges have a definite double serration which is sometimes a little deep. The green petioles are long, slender, and about 4 cm long. 'Muro gawa' is hardy and a fairly vigorous grower but not totally upright. With age, the side branches become somewhat pendulous and the top slows its rate of growth. The mature tree is round-topped with pendulous outer branches. Old trees grow to 6 m tall and, if not trimmed, spread to 3-4 m."
  },
